## Harness usage

```text
/orchestrator → default entry point: full plan → work → review → PR loop
                with human gates (worth it for 3+ phase work)
/plan         → Plans.md from requirements (planner subagent, opus)
/work N       → implement Phase N (coder + tester subagents, TDD commits)
/review       → 4-lens gate (reviewer subagent, opus)
/release      → 🔒 PR + docs (must type manually)
/setup        → bootstrap a new subproject
```

## Subagents

`@agent-explorer @agent-planner @agent-coder @agent-tester @agent-reviewer @agent-documenter`

- planner / reviewer: opus (expensive decisions)
- explorer / coder / tester / documenter: sonnet (execution)

## MCP / external services

(Add your `.mcp.json` configs here as documentation, not the actual tokens.)

## Safety nets installed

- `PreToolUse` Bash guard (blocks destructive commands) — `.claude/hooks/block-destructive.sh`
- `PreToolUse` Edit/Write guard (blocks secret writes) — `.claude/hooks/protect-secrets.sh`
- `PostToolUse` Edit/Write auto-format (Python, ruff/black) — `.claude/hooks/post-edit-lint.sh`
- `SubagentStart/Stop` agent activity announce + log — `.claude/hooks/announce-agent.sh`
- All four are wired in `.claude/settings.json`; regression suite: `bash .claude/hooks/tests/run-tests.sh`
- Per-subproject `.claude/` overrides take precedence (don't load this CLAUDE.md inside them)
